// Blizzard's map frame OpenMap hosts in (`WorldMapFrame`), and the game's tooltip beside a pin, as `worldMap.lua`
// reads them: the frame isn't declared by the client's API. Nothing is written to it: its scripts are hooked.
import Client from "$client"

// The world map's canvas, where pins stand; nil before Blizzard's map is made.
public function canvas(): any Client.Frame | nil
// The map the world map shows (`WorldMapFrame:GetMapID()`); 0 while it doesn't show.
public function shownMap(): Integer
// `run` is called when the world map shows or hides and when the map it shows changes. Once; `forget` takes it away.
public function listen(run: () => nil)
public function forget()
// The game's tooltip beside a pin: its first line the title, in white, the others under it.
public function tip(owner: any Client.Frame, lines: Array<String>)
public function untip()
